WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.173
Did I hear someone in
that prior panel say,

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.210
if you're against toxic maximalism,

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:10.377
you're against Bitcoin and
you're against freedom?

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.510
Yeah, that's some bullshit.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:19.830
We got 'em warmed up.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.800
Few figures in the Bitcoin community,

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.220
are as controversial and
visionary as Erik Voorhees,

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.580
founder and CEO of the
cryptocurrency exchange ShapeShift.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.910
He drew cheers and occasional
boos at Bitcoin 2021,

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:36.420
the recent blockbuster
conference in Miami.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.060
Back when cryptocurrency
was in its infancy,

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.000
Voorhees was helping to popularize

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.396
Bitcoin's unique attributes

00:00:42.396 --> 00:00:46.700
with an unregulated online
casino called SatoshiDICE.

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.020
After he sold, Voorhees
was investigated by the SEC

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.470
and paid a $50,000 fine.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.600
Observing that the
investigators didn't even

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.317
seem to understand Bitcoin,

00:00:56.317 --> 00:00:59.317
"As much as I hated government
before," he recalled,

00:00:59.317 --> 00:01:02.117
"then I was like, 'Man, this
is what these people do,

00:01:02.117 --> 00:01:05.030
"'go around ruining
innocent people's lives.'"

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.830
Unlike Bitcoin maximalists,
who insist that Bitcoin

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:11.410
is the only cryptocurrency
with any viable future,

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.520
Voorhees maintains that other
coins do serve a purpose.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.601
I love seeing all the crypto
projects coming together

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:19.290
with the financial institutions.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.080
I think some people in
crypto don't like that,

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.390
but I see crypto taking over the world

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:24.240
and that doesn't happen without

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.020
bringing basically everyone into the tent.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:29.600
In 2017 as fees on the
network were climbing,

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.700
he controversially backed
an unsuccessful attempt

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.220
to scale up Bitcoin's ability
to process transactions,

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:39.008
which critics said would have
weakened the network security

00:01:39.008 --> 00:01:40.910
and decentralized structure.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:44.050
At the Bitcoin 2021 conference in Miami,

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:46.810
Voorhees talked to Reason
about the immense growth,

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.758
not just in the market
caps of cryptocurrencies,

00:01:49.758 --> 00:01:52.670
but in their economic
and cultural legitimacy,

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:55.030
the ways in which they
challenged central banks

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.410
and political power,

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:59.110
and why he believes in multiple coins and

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:01.753
continuing innovation in digital currency.

